The $"M"(n, p_1, ..., p_k)$ distribution counts occurrences of each outcome in $n$ independent trials with outcome probabilities $p_1, ..., p_k$ summing to $1$:
$
  p_(n_1, ..., n_k) = binom(n, n_1, ..., n_k) p_1^(n_1) dots.c p_k^(n_k)
$
on $Omega = {(n_1, ..., n_k) in NN^k : sum_(i=1)^k n_i = n}$.
